    "body": "## Problem\n\nWhen an edit leaves the buffer with a single empty line, incremental sync assumes the whole buffer was deleted and excludes the EOL of the last deleted line, even when the remaining empty line was not deleted. E.g. `Gdd` on `{'', 'foo'}` sends range 1:0-1:3 instead of 1:0-2:0, so the server keeps an extra empty line. This is what the yank/put in #36653 hits.\n\n## Solution\n\nOnly apply the empty-buffer special case from #29904 when every line was deleted, and return an empty range when no lines changed (so an empty insertion stays a no-op).\n\nFixes #36653\n",
